From 089acfae4735f1b76d2fa2723cdbc44786647c4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:01:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: count Resist Poison potions from zero in the inventory
 power

The 'collect Resistance pots if not immune' reward in
borg_power_inventory() loops 'for (; k < 4 && k < BI_ARESPOIS; k++)'
without resetting k, so it starts from wherever the previous loop left
it: the low-calorie food count (capped at 15), or the Cure Serious
Wounds count when cut or poisoned.  A borg carrying four or more apples,
slime molds or similar therefore put no value at all on its Resist
Poison potions.

Reset k before the loop, as the neighbouring reward loops do.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#184.

(cherry picked from commit 5e8d4c5e6c1006ce4c90e21a973b0f95bb9fa0db)
---
 src/borg/borg-power.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-power.c b/src/borg/borg-power.c
index 26f80885b..277c3bccc 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-power.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-power.c
@@ -1185,6 +1185,7 @@ static int32_t borg_power_inventory(void)
             && borg.trait[BI_MAXCLEVEL] < borg_cfg[BORG_MUNCHKIN_LEVEL]) {
             /* Do not carry these until later */
         } else {
+            k = 0;
             for (; k < 4 && k < borg.trait[BI_ARESPOIS]; k++)
                 value += 300L;
         }
